# LOVE runtime binaries live outside the repo
*.exe
*.dll
*.love

# The Steamworks SDK, and anything built against it, must never land here. The
# blanket *.dll rule above already covers the two binaries; these are named
# anyway, because the licence question is not a matter of tidiness. Valve's grant
# is for local development use, the only redistribution it permits is
# redistributable_bin alongside a game in object form, and it is terminable at
# will -- none of which can be reconciled with Apache-2.0. That includes
# luasteam's own vendored sdk/ tree, which is Valve's and not luasteam's to
# relicense. See docs/NETWORKING.md, "Building luasteam".
steam_api64.dll
steam_api.dll
libsteam_api.so
libsteam_api.dylib
luasteam.dll
luasteam.so
steam_appid.txt
sdk/
SteamworksSDK/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor / tooling
.claude/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch output: screenshots, exported maps, profiling dumps
_scratch/
_shots/

# Release artifacts from scripts/package.ps1 — fused exe, .love, staging.
build/

# H1: game projects are their own repos, not this one's content. The engine
# creates them here by default (`love .` → Projects → create).
projects/

# The engine generates every texture at runtime. If media ever appears here it
# was not put there on purpose, so keep it out by default.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.wav
*.ogg
*.mp3
*.ttf
*.otf
*.xcf
*.psd

# ...except the handful of README screenshots, which are procedural output.
!docs/media/*.png
